## 4. Summary

  Files: 19.
  Total lines: 1927.
  Files over 256: 0. wasm_hyg.oot:56-57, 86 reports
    "None. Zero emit files over 256. Zero runtime C files
    over 256."
  Closest to cap: none within 30 lines. Largest audit is
    wasm_coord.oot at 226 (still 30 under cap).

  12-role master wave (12 files, all [x]):
    Owns the ship bar (wasm_phalanx.oot:7-15), disjoint
    write paths (wasm_phalanx.oot:62), and the frozen API
    (wasm_phalanx.oot:19-30). C emit + gcc stays the
    everyday path (wasm_phalanx.oot:5, wasm_phalanx.oot:78).

  COORD-wave (3 files, all [x]):
    wasm_coord.oot drives the parent rebuild, then fans out
    the if-fold review to existing roles
    (wasm_coord.oot:191-202 "Order"). Adds wasm_harn2.oot
    for the const if-false fixture. Re-uses wasm_harn.oot
    for the const if-true fixture. Locks if-true/if-false
    smokes (wasm_coord.oot:76, wasm_coord.oot:88). Hostile
    IDENT if stays dummy (wasm_coord.oot:97-100,
    wasm_pv1.oot:135-140).

  Loop-12 wave (5 files, all [?]):
    Adds five named const-print folds beyond the master
    print-lit and hello greet fold: seventeen println,
    if (!(1==x)), if 1!=x || 3!=3, if (1!=x && 3!=4),
    if 1<x && 3<4 (wasm_arch.oot:6-10). Five detector .oo
    files back the picks (wasm_emit_pick_print.oo:32,
    wasm_emit_pick_if.oo:62-65). wasm_pipe.oot:5-9 names
    the five detectors. Hostile IDENT forms miss
    (wasm_arch.oot:12, wasm_pipe.oot:11, wasm_qa.oot:20-24,
    wasm_sk1.oot:13-32). Isolation is checked
    (wasm_sk2.oot:14-19).

## 5. Gaps

  Loop-12 wave role assignment: pending. The master plan
    does not list ARCH, PIPE, QA, SK1, or SK2
    (wasm_phalanx.oot:39-71). No audit file on disk names
    the wave that owns these five roles. The five files
    are [?] for that reason.

  Post-phalanx sibling code is not in the master. The
    master (wasm_phalanx.oot:39-71) names `wasm_emit.oo`
    and the fold and picks implicitly through DE1 and
    INT, but the new 28-detector print pick and 52-detector
    if pick (wasm_emit_pick_print.oo:14-72, wasm_emit_pick_if.oo:14-120)
    are post-master. No audit file says which wave owns
    them. They live in ooda/oodac/ and are driven by
    wasm_emit.oo:56-59.

  wasm_qa.oot has no explicit "Status:" line. Its last
    line is wasm_qa.oot:28 "Magic 0061736d01000000. Not
    WAT. Not oodac.wasm4." Status is taken from that line
    plus its "Verdict" intent at wasm_qa.oot:26-27.

Status: 14 of 19 are [x]. 5 are [?]. Wave 3 (Loop-12)
  awaits assignment.
